</section>
<section id="S6.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S6.SS6.4" class="ltx_text">VI-F</span> </span><span id="S6.SS6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Demonstration on Robots</span></h3>

<div id="S6.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we deploy our algorithms in real-world environments to validate the effectiveness of SGF. Since Vicsek uses periodic boundary conditions that cannot be implemented in the real world, we focus on the other tasks instead. Specifically, we use Limo robots as agents, controlled via the Robot Operating System (ROS) system, with real-time environmental states captured by Nokov motion capture system. The setup of the task is shown in Fig. <a href="#S6.F6" title="Fig. 6 ‣ VI-E The Impact of Different Numbers of Agents ‣ VI Experiments ‣ Symmetry-Guided Multi-Agent Inverse Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. The Rendezvous involves 5 agents, while the Pursuit consists of 4 predators and 1 prey. Without loss of generality, we choose MA-AIRL and S-MA-AIRL for real-world validation, using cumulative distance as the performance metric. The results, as presented in Table <a href="#S6.T3" title="TABLE III ‣ VI-E The Impact of Different Numbers of Agents ‣ VI Experiments ‣ Symmetry-Guided Multi-Agent Inverse Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III</span></a>, show that the algorithms using SGF complete tasks faster in both tasks, confirming the effectiveness of our method in real-world applications.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">VII </span><span id="S7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Conclusions</span></h2>

<div id="S7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This paper aims to address the problem of sample inefficiency in MIRL. We provide the first proof that leveraging the inherent symmetry in MAS can recover more accurate reward functions. Based on this theory, we propose a novel framework for multi-agent adversarial IRL algorithms, termed the Symmetry-Guided Framework (SGF). Experimental results show that our framework significantly enhances the performance of the algorithms, achieving superior convergence rewards. Furthermore, the policies learned with the recovered rewards have been deployed in physical multi-robot systems, further validating the effectiveness of our framework in real-world scenarios.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Appendixes</h2>

<div id="Sx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <math id="Sx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>-function and <math id="Sx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>-function of a policy <math id="Sx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> in MG <math id="Sx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}\cup r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}\cup r</annotation></semantics></math> are defined as:</p>
<table id="Sx1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q^{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>𝝅</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q^{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma\sum_{s^{\prime},\bm{a}^{\prime}}\bm{\pi}(\bm{a}^{\prime}|s^{\prime})P(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})Q^{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s^{\prime},\bm{a}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>𝝅</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma\sum_{s^{\prime},\bm{a}^{\prime}}\bm{\pi}(\bm{a}^{\prime}|s^{\prime})P(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})Q^{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s^{\prime},\bm{a}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+r(s,\bm{a})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+r(s,\bm{a}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V^{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>𝝅</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V^{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{\bm{a}}\bm{\pi}(\bm{a}|s)Q^{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>𝝅</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{\bm{a}}\bm{\pi}(\bm{a}|s)Q^{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">If policy <math id="Sx1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\pi}_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\pi}_{E}</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal policy under reward <math id="Sx1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, then we can derive the following equations:</p>
<table id="Sx1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})-V^{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s)=0,\quad if\ \bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)&gt;0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>𝝅</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})-V^{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s)=0,\quad if\ \bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})-V^{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s)\leq 0,\quad if\ \bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>𝝅</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})-V^{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s)\leq 0,\quad if\ \bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>-function satisfies the condition of equations (<a href="#Sx1.E4" title="In Appendixes ‣ Symmetry-Guided Multi-Agent Inverse Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) and (<a href="#Sx1.E5" title="In Appendixes ‣ Symmetry-Guided Multi-Agent Inverse Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) if and only if there exists <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{S}}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{S}}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in\mathbb{R}^{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in\mathbb{R}^{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that:</span></p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})=-\zeta\mathbb{I}_{\{\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0\}}+V(s)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>ζ</mi><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝝅</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})=-\zeta\mathbb{I}_{\{\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0\}}+V(s).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof:</h6>
<div id="Sx1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first show that if <math id="Sx1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})</annotation></semantics></math> has this form, then the equations (<a href="#Sx1.E4" title="In Appendixes ‣ Symmetry-Guided Multi-Agent Inverse Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) and (<a href="#Sx1.E5" title="In Appendixes ‣ Symmetry-Guided Multi-Agent Inverse Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) are satisfied, and then converse. Assuming <math id="Sx1.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})=-\zeta\mathbb{I}_{\{\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0\}}+V(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>ζ</mi><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝝅</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})=-\zeta\mathbb{I}_{\{\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0\}}+V(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, then we can get <math id="Sx1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s)=\sum_{\bm{a}}\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)Q^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})=V(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s)=\sum_{\bm{a}}\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)Q^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})=V(s)</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="Sx1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Sx1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})=V^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})=V^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, which satisfies equation (<a href="#Sx1.E4" title="In Appendixes ‣ Symmetry-Guided Multi-Agent Inverse Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). If <math id="Sx1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Sx1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})=V^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s)-\zeta\leq V^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})=V^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s)-\zeta\leq V^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, which satisfies equation (<a href="#Sx1.E5" title="In Appendixes ‣ Symmetry-Guided Multi-Agent Inverse Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). For the converse, assume equations (<a href="#Sx1.E4" title="In Appendixes ‣ Symmetry-Guided Multi-Agent Inverse Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) and (<a href="#Sx1.E5" title="In Appendixes ‣ Symmetry-Guided Multi-Agent Inverse Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) hold. We take <math id="Sx1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(s)=V^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(s)=V^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta=V^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s)-Q^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta=V^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s)-Q^{\bm{\pi}_{E}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then we can give the proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Feasible Reward Set) ‣ IV-A Problem Definition ‣ IV Symmetry-Guided Multi-Agent Inverse Reinforcement Learning ‣ Symmetry-Guided Multi-Agent Inverse Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> as follows.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof:</h6>
<div id="Sx1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">From the definition of <math id="Sx1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>-function and <math id="Sx1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>-function, we have:</span></p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})=r(s,\bm{a})+\sum\nolimits_{s^{\prime}}P(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})V(s^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>𝝅</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})=r(s,\bm{a})+\sum\nolimits_{s^{\prime}}P(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})V(s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we can get:</span></p>
<table id="Sx1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r(s,\bm{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r(s,\bm{a})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=Q^{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})-\gamma\sum\nolimits_{s^{\prime}}P(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})V(s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>𝝅</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=Q^{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathcal{M}\cup r}(s,\bm{a})-\gamma\sum\nolimits_{s^{\prime}}P(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})V(s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\zeta\mathbb{I}_{\{\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0\}}+V(s)-\gamma\sum\nolimits_{s^{\prime}}P(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})V(s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>ζ</mi><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝝅</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mstyle><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\zeta\mathbb{I}_{\{\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0\}}+V(s)-\gamma\sum\nolimits_{s^{\prime}}P(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})V(s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we provide the proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Error Propagation) ‣ IV-B Error Propagation ‣ IV Symmetry-Guided Multi-Agent Inverse Reinforcement Learning ‣ Symmetry-Guided Multi-Agent Inverse Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.1.1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof:</h6>
<div id="Sx1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can rewrite the reward functions <math id="Sx1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</span></p>
<table id="Sx1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r(s,\bm{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r(s,\bm{a})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\zeta\mathbb{I}_{\{\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0\}}+V(s)-\gamma\sum\nolimits_{s^{\prime}}P(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})V(s^{\prime})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>ζ</mi><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝝅</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mstyle><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\zeta\mathbb{I}_{\{\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0\}}+V(s)-\gamma\sum\nolimits_{s^{\prime}}P(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})V(s^{\prime}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{r}(s,\bm{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{r}(s,\bm{a})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\hat{\zeta}\mathbb{I}_{\{\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0\}}+\hat{V}(s)-\gamma\sum\nolimits_{s^{\prime}}\hat{P}(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})\hat{V}(s^{\prime})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mstyle><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\hat{\zeta}\mathbb{I}_{\{\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0\}}+\hat{V}(s)-\gamma\sum\nolimits_{s^{\prime}}\hat{P}(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})\hat{V}(s^{\prime}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Without loss of generality, we can choose <math id="Sx1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\hat{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\hat{V}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.p8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{\zeta}=\zeta\mathbb{I}_{\{\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mi>𝕀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝝅</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\zeta}=\zeta\mathbb{I}_{\{\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0\}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="Sx1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r(s,\bm{a})-\hat{r}(s,\bm{a})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r(s,\bm{a})-\hat{r}(s,\bm{a})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\zeta\mathbb{I}_{\{\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0\}}\mathbb{I}_{\{\hat{\bm{\pi}}(s,\bm{a})&gt;0\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mi>𝕀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝝅</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>𝕀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\zeta\mathbb{I}_{\{\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0\}}\mathbb{I}_{\{\hat{\bm{\pi}}(s,\bm{a})&gt;0\}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\gamma\sum\nolimits_{s^{\prime}}V(s^{\prime})(P(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})-\hat{P}(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a}))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mstyle><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\gamma\sum\nolimits_{s^{\prime}}V(s^{\prime})(P(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})-\hat{P}(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">The results follow by taking the absolute value and applying triangle inequality.
∎</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, we present the proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Symmetry-Guided MIRL Improvement) ‣ IV-C Symmetry-Guided MIRL ‣ IV Symmetry-Guided Multi-Agent Inverse Reinforcement Learning ‣ Symmetry-Guided Multi-Agent Inverse Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof:</h6>
<div id="Sx1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="Sx1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,\bm{a})\in\tau_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>E</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,\bm{a})\in\tau_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="Sx1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}(g\bm{a}|gs)=\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}(\bm{a}|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>E</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>E</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}(g\bm{a}|gs)=\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}(\bm{a}|s)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{P}^{\mathcal{G}}(gs^{\prime}|gs,g\bm{a})=\hat{P}^{\mathcal{G}}(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{P}^{\mathcal{G}}(gs^{\prime}|gs,g\bm{a})=\hat{P}^{\mathcal{G}}(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="Sx1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{M}}^{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{M}}^{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="Sx1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant MG\R. For <math id="Sx1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,\bm{a})\in\tau_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,\bm{a})\in\tau_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="Sx1.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}(\bm{a}|s)=\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>E</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}(\bm{a}|s)=\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{P}^{\mathcal{G}}(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})=\hat{P}(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{P}^{\mathcal{G}}(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})=\hat{P}(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Sx1.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{P}^{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{P}^{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the transition model formed from <math id="Sx1.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>E</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The Error Propagation of the MIRL problem <math id="Sx1.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{B}^{\mathcal{G}}=({\hat{\mathcal{M}}^{\mathcal{G}},\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>E</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{B}^{\mathcal{G}}=({\hat{\mathcal{M}}^{\mathcal{G}},\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}})</annotation></semantics></math> is:</span></p>
<table id="Sx1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|r(s,\bm{a})-\hat{r}^{\mathcal{G}}(s,\bm{a})|\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|r(s,\bm{a})-\hat{r}^{\mathcal{G}}(s,\bm{a})|\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\zeta\mathbb{I}_{\{\bm{\pi}_{E}(a|s)=0\}}\mathbb{I}_{\{\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}(a|s)&gt;0\}}+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mi>𝕀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝝅</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>𝕀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\zeta\mathbb{I}_{\{\bm{\pi}_{E}(a|s)=0\}}\mathbb{I}_{\{\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}(a|s)&gt;0\}}+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma\sum_{s^{\prime}}|V(s^{\prime})(P(s^{\prime}|s,a)-\hat{P}^{\mathcal{G}}(s^{\prime}|s,a))|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma\sum_{s^{\prime}}|V(s^{\prime})(P(s^{\prime}|s,a)-\hat{P}^{\mathcal{G}}(s^{\prime}|s,a))|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">We denote the difference between the upper bounds of the two Error Propagation as:</span></p>
<table id="Sx1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\delta=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\zeta\mathbb{I}_{\{\bm{\pi}(\bm{a}|s)=0\}}(\mathbb{I}_{\{\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)&gt;0\}}-\mathbb{I}_{\{\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}(\bm{a}|s)&gt;0\}})+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝝅</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\zeta\mathbb{I}_{\{\bm{\pi}(\bm{a}|s)=0\}}(\mathbb{I}_{\{\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)&gt;0\}}-\mathbb{I}_{\{\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}(\bm{a}|s)&gt;0\}})+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma\sum_{s^{\prime}}(|\Delta\hat{P}(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})|-|\Delta\hat{P}^{\mathcal{G}}(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})|)|V(s^{\prime})|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma\sum_{s^{\prime}}(|\Delta\hat{P}(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})|-|\Delta\hat{P}^{\mathcal{G}}(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})|)|V(s^{\prime})|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="Sx1.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=|r(s,\bm{a})-\hat{r}(s,\bm{a})|-|r(s,\bm{a})-\hat{r}^{\mathcal{G}}(s,\bm{a})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=|r(s,\bm{a})-\hat{r}(s,\bm{a})|-|r(s,\bm{a})-\hat{r}^{\mathcal{G}}(s,\bm{a})|</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Sx1.p11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\hat{P}=P-\hat{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\hat{P}=P-\hat{P}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.p11.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\hat{P}^{\mathcal{G}}=P-\hat{P}^{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\hat{P}^{\mathcal{G}}=P-\hat{P}^{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We will discuss the two terms of <math id="Sx1.p11.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> separately.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">The first term can only be positive if <math id="Sx1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, so we begin with this condition. When <math id="Sx1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,\bm{a})\in\tau_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,\bm{a})\in\tau_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="Sx1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\pi}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, there will be no samples of the pair <math id="Sx1.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,\bm{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,\bm{a})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="Sx1.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies <math id="Sx1.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and similarly <math id="Sx1.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\pi}_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}(\bm{a}|s)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>E</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\pi}_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}(\bm{a}|s)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, the first term is 0. When <math id="Sx1.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,\bm{a})\in\tau_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>E</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,\bm{a})\in\tau_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,\bm{a})\notin\tau_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,\bm{a})\notin\tau_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="Sx1.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}(\bm{a}|s)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Based on the <math id="Sx1.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant MG\R, there exists a <math id="Sx1.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Sx1.p12.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g^{-1}s,g^{-1}\bm{a})\in\tau_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g^{-1}s,g^{-1}\bm{a})\in\tau_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, <math id="Sx1.p12.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\pi}_{E}(g^{-1}s|g^{-1}\bm{a})=\bm{\pi}_{E}(s|\bm{a})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\pi}_{E}(g^{-1}s|g^{-1}\bm{a})=\bm{\pi}_{E}(s|\bm{a})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, which leads to <math id="Sx1.p12.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}(g^{-1}\bm{a}|g^{-1}s)=\bm{\pi}_{E}(g^{-1}s|g^{-1}\bm{a})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>E</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{\pi}}_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}(g^{-1}\bm{a}|g^{-1}s)=\bm{\pi}_{E}(g^{-1}s|g^{-1}\bm{a})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, the first term is positive. Overall, the first term is non-negative.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">According to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>, <a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>, we can obtain the bounds:</span></p>
<table id="Sx1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall(s,\bm{a})\in\tau,|P(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})-\hat{P}(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})|\leq\frac{C}{\sqrt{D(s,\bm{a})}}&lt;1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>C</mi><msqrt><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall(s,\bm{a})\in\tau,|P(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})-\hat{P}(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})|\leq\frac{C}{\sqrt{D(s,\bm{a})}}&lt;1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall(s,\bm{a})\notin\tau,|P(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})-\hat{P}(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})|\leq 1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall(s,\bm{a})\notin\tau,|P(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})-\hat{P}(s^{\prime}|s,\bm{a})|\leq 1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="Sx1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant and <math id="Sx1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(s,\bm{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(s,\bm{a})</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of of <math id="Sx1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,\bm{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,\bm{a})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="Sx1.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the second term, when <math id="Sx1.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,\bm{a})\in\tau_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,\bm{a})\in\tau_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, the second term is zero. When <math id="Sx1.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,\bm{a})\in\tau_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>E</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,\bm{a})\in\tau_{E}^{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,\bm{a})\notin\tau_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,\bm{a})\notin\tau_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, the upper bound difference of the second term is <math id="Sx1.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{C}{\sqrt{D^{\mathcal{G}}(s,\bm{a})}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>C</mi><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{C}{\sqrt{D^{\mathcal{G}}(s,\bm{a})}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the second term is non-negative. In summary, <math id="Sx1.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
